    {
     "ord": 2,
     "period": {
      "start": "1939-09-06",
      "end": "1939-09-10"
     },
     "periodStartPrecision": "day",
     "periodEndPrecision": "day",
     "heading": {
      "zh-Hant": "九月的撤退決定",
      "en": "Retreat decisions in September"
     },
     "body": {
      "zh-Hant": "IPN 專題寫到，9月6日晚間法布里齊下令第24步兵師撤到維斯沃卡河後方，接著在7日決定退向桑河一線；他指揮的部隊自9月6日起稱 Armia „Małopolska”（小波蘭軍）。文中還說，他後來又命令部分部隊撤往普熱梅希爾。專題作者對這些後撤決定持批評態度，但本檔只記錄其所述的命令與日期，不採其評語。",
      "en": "The IPN portal reports that on the evening of 6 September Fabrycy ordered the 24th Infantry Division to withdraw behind the Wisłok and then, on 7 September, a retreat to the San line; his force was called Armia „Małopolska” from 6 September. It adds that he later ordered some units to fall back to Przemyśl. The author is critical of these withdrawals, but this entry records only the orders and dates described, not the judgement."
     },
